UPDATE companies SET description='Food Northwest operates from Portland, Oregon, where it was organized in 1914 as the Northwest Canners Association. Incorporated in Oregon in 1922, the trade association evolved through mergers and name changes — becoming the Northwest Food Processors Association in 1969 and rebranding as Food Northwest in 2018. The organization serves the food processing industry across Idaho, Oregon, and Washington from its office positioned midway between the three state capitals.

The association provides advocacy, training, technical resources, and networking for 350-plus member companies. Its professional staff manages government relations on food policy, environmental regulation, energy, and workforce issues; develops tools such as the Listeria Control Checklist and Sanitary Design Guide; and produces the annual Food Northwest Process & Packaging Expo, which marked its 50th edition in 2022. Five volunteer committees and task forces address sector-specific challenges, while the Education and Research Institute, incorporated in 2007, supports scholarships and workforce development.

Membership spans international brands, regional processors, and family-owned operations handling fruits, vegetables, seafood, dairy, bakery, specialty foods, and juices. Processor members represent nearly all food categories, while supplier members provide equipment, ingredients, and services to the industry. The association''s Endowment Fund, established in 1989, funds food-science education at colleges in the three states.

Food Northwest was founded to advance the region''s ability to produce and deliver safe, wholesome food to global markets. Its core priorities — food policy, government relations, environmental stewardship, energy, education, and sustainability — are set annually by the membership and affirmed by the Board of Directors, positioning the association as an authoritative voice for the Pacific Northwest food processing cluster.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Government affairs advocacy", "Food policy and regulation monitoring", "Environmental affairs and sustainability programs", "Energy policy and resources management", "Workforce education and training", "Industry events and expositions", "Technical resource development", "Member networking committees and task forces", "Scholarship and workforce development programs", "Issue management and crisis response", "Professional development and leadership programs", "Print and online industry publications"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Seafood processing", "Dairy processing", "Bakery", "Specialty foods", "Juice and beverage processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the nation''s largest food processing trade associations with 350+ members", "Authoritative voice for food policy, environmental, and energy advocacy in the Pacific Northwest", "Annual Process & Packaging Expo celebrating 50 years in 2022", "Education and Research Institute funding scholarships and workforce development", "Technical resources including Listeria Control Checklist and Sanitary Design Guide"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1914 as Northwest Canners Association -> /about", "Incorporated in Oregon 1922 -> /about", "Renamed Northwest Food Processors Association 1969 -> /about", "Rebranded Food Northwest 2018 -> /about", "Headquarters Portland, Oregon -> /about and /", "350+ members -> /about", "Serves Idaho, Oregon, Washington -> /about", "Core priorities: food policy, government relations, environmental, energy, education, sustainability -> /about", "Five volunteer committees/task forces -> /about", "Annual Process & Packaging Expo, 50th edition 2022 -> /about", "Education and Research Institute incorporated 2007 -> /about", "Endowment Fund established 1989 -> /about", "Listeria Control Checklist Version 2.0 -> / and /about", "Sanitary Design Guide -> / and /about", "Membership includes international brands, regional, family businesses -> /about", "Processor membership opened to nearly all food products 1999 -> /about", "Associate members accepted 1985 -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db and /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Food Northwest, formerly the Northwest Food Processors Association (NWFPA), is a trade association organized to advance the ability of the food industry to produce and deliver wholesome, safe food from the Pacific Northwest to the world.", "founded_year": "1914", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/480320/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-northwest' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Tech, based in Rockland, Massachusetts, operates as a design-build firm specializing in food processing plants and cold storage facilities. The company is a subsidiary of EMCOR Group, Inc., a Fortune 500 mechanical and electrical construction leader. Bob Ross, P.E., serves as president.

The firm provides end-to-end services including facility planning, preconstruction, architecture, engineering, and construction management. It does not self-perform construction, instead managing competitive bidding among subcontractors. A notable project is a 190,000-square-foot cheese production facility capable of processing two million pounds of milk per day, featuring robotic packing and palletizing.

Food Tech serves dairy, fresh food, frozen food, USDA meat plants, and cold storage sectors. Its clients range from large publicly traded companies to smaller regional processors, distributors, retailers, and wholesalers. Offices in Boston and Milwaukee support a national footprint.

The company differentiates itself through a single-source design-build model that delivers a guaranteed maximum price early, returns savings from competitive bids, and maintains in-house architecture and engineering. Its safety program is described as award-winning and industry-leading.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Facility planning", "Preconstruction", "Architecture and engineering", "Construction management", "Design-build project delivery", "Feasibility studies", "Competitive bidding of trades", "At-risk construction management", "Sanitary facility design", "Material handling systems", "Refrigeration systems", "Energy-efficient design", "Environmentally sustainable design"], "industries": ["Dairy", "Fresh food", "Frozen food", "USDA meat plants", "Cold storage", "Food processing", "Food distribution", "Retail", "Wholesale"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source design-build delivery with guaranteed maximum price early", "Competitive bidding for all trades with return of savings to client", "In-house architecture and engineering across all disciplines", "No self-performed construction, ensuring unbiased material and system recommendations", "Award-winning safety program"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Rockland, Massachusetts -> db", "Part of EMCOR Group, Inc. -> /about-us", "Bob Ross, P.E., President -> /", "Design-build services for food process plants and cold storage -> /", "190,000 sq ft cheese facility processing 2M lbs milk/day -> /", "Offices in Boston and Milwaukee -> /about-us", "Services: facility planning, preconstruction, architecture, engineering, construction management -> /services", "Industries: dairy, fresh food, frozen food, USDA meat plants, cold storage -> /services", "No self-performed construction -> /services", "Guaranteed maximum price early, competitive bidding with savings return -> /about-us", "In-house architecture and engineering -> /about-us", "Award-winning safety program -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Food Tech specializes in the planning/ engineering/construction of food process plants and cold storage facilities.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-tech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Truck Builders of Phoenix operates from Glendale, Arizona, where it designs, fabricates, and sells custom mobile kitchens. The company focuses on food trucks, concession trailers, carts, and kiosks, along with stainless steel fabrication for commercial kitchens. No founding year or ownership details are disclosed in public materials.

The shop builds complete food trucks and trailers from the ground up, handling design, permits, blueprints, and custom stainless steel work such as exhaust hoods, cabinets, shelves, and holding tanks. It also sells and installs new and used NSF‑approved cooking equipment, refrigeration, exhaust systems, work tables, and sinks, and offers a rental program for kitchen equipment. Repair services cover commercial refrigeration, cooking gear, exhaust systems, trailers, electrical, plumbing, and AC, with a 24‑hour turnaround and parts stocked for major brands. Fire suppression inspection, installation, and repair are also provided.

Customers include food‑truck entrepreneurs, chefs, and mobile‑food vendors nationwide; the company notes its units operate across the country. It also serves brick‑and‑mortar restaurants needing stainless steel fabrication or equipment. The business caters to both new builds and remodels of existing trucks.

The company differentiates itself by guaranteeing that every truck and trailer passes initial health inspections in any city or state, beating competitors'' written quotes by 10%, and offering seller financing at 0% interest for 12 months with half down. Its repair experience informs equipment selection, ensuring compatibility in the tight confines of a mobile kitchen.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom food truck manufacturing", "Food trailer manufacturing", "Custom concession trailer building", "Food truck design", "Food truck repair (24-hour service)", "Food truck remodel and renovation", "Food truck customization", "Stainless steel fabrication (cabinets, shelves, exhaust hoods, holding tanks)", "Commercial kitchen equipment sales (new and used NSF-approved)", "Kitchen equipment rental", "Permits and blueprints service", "Fire suppression inspection, installation, and repair", "Trailer repair", "RV and food truck AC repair", "Custom installation and fabrication", "Equipment financing", "Food truck consignment", "Used restaurant equipment sales", "Airstream food and concession trailer sales", "Coffee trailer sales"], "industries": ["Mobile food service", "Food truck industry", "Commercial kitchens", "Restaurant industry", "Concession and catering"], "materials": ["Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Guaranteed to pass initial health inspections in any city or state", "Beats competitors'' written quotes by 10%", "Seller financing at 0% interest for 12 months with 50% down", "24-hour food truck repair service with parts on hand for major brands", "Repair experience used to advise on equipment compatibility"], "facts_used": ["Located in Glendale, Arizona -> db", "Specializes in stainless steel fabrication for food trucks and commercial kitchens -> db", "Builds custom food trucks, trailers, carts, and kiosks -> /", "Offers 24-hour food truck repair service -> /", "Sells new and used NSF-approved equipment -> /", "Provides permits and blueprints service -> /", "Offers kitchen equipment rental -> /", "Provides financing with 0% interest for 12 months with half down -> /", "Guarantees to pass health inspections -> /", "Beats competitors'' written quotes by 10% -> /", "Repair experience informs equipment selection -> /", "Fire suppression inspection, installation, and repair -> /", "Trailer repair and RV/food truck AC repair -> /", "Custom stainless steel fabrication (cabinets, shelves, exhaust hoods, holding tanks) -> /", "Food truck design, remodel, renovation, customization -> /", "Airstream food and concession trailers for sale -> /", "Coffee trailers for sale -> /", "Food truck consignment and used restaurant equipment sales -> /", "Units seen all over the country -> /", "Serves food truck entrepreneurs, chefs, mobile food vendors nationwide -> /", "Also serves brick-and-mortar restaurants -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Food Truck Builders of Phoenix, we specialize in fabricating customized mobile kitchens for one of the nation''s fastest-growing industries. We build everything from food trucks and trailers, to carts and kiosks.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-truck-builders-of-phoenix' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Truck Headquarters USA operates from Clinton Township, Michigan, serving as an online specialist for food‑truck kitchen equipment and appliances. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or the names of its founders.

The business stocks a curated selection of commercial‑grade equipment from brands such as Cookshack commercial smokers and Brood nitro coffee machines, targeting the specific spatial and power constraints of mobile and commissary kitchens. It functions as a distributor rather than a manufacturer, managing inventory, order fulfillment, and free shipping on most items, while explicitly stating it does not provide on‑site installation.

Its customer base consists of food‑truck entrepreneurs, food‑trailer and food‑cart operators, and commissary‑kitchen managers. The company’s educational content — covering topics from generator sizing to menu pricing — is aimed at both startup and established mobile‑food businesses across multiple states.

Food Truck Headquarters USA differentiates itself through hands‑on industry experience: its staff have built and operated food trucks, trailers, and commissary kitchens, allowing them to advise on equipment fit and functionality. The firm also publishes a library of how‑to guides and product comparisons to help buyers make informed purchasing decisions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Equipment distribution", "Product selection consulting", "Order management and shipment tracking", "Educational content publishing"], "industries": ["Food truck", "Food trailer", "Food cart", "Commissary kitchen", "Mobile food service"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Cookshack commercial smokers", "Brood nitro coffee machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free shipping on most equipment and appliances", "Staff with hands\u2011on food\u2011truck build and operations experience", "Educational resource library for mobile\u2011food operators", "Personalized product selection support via phone or chat"], "facts_used": ["Location: Clinton Township, Michigan -> db", "Business model: distributor of food\u2011truck equipment (Cookshack, Brood) -> /about-us", "Free shipping on most equipment -> /", "No on\u2011site installation provided -> /about-us", "Staff have food\u2011truck build and operations experience -> /about-us", "Educational resources published for mobile\u2011food operators -> /about-us, /", "Target customers: food\u2011truck entrepreneurs, trailer/cart operators, commissary kitchens -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We stock a select range of top-brand commercial kitchen equipment and supplies that are either designed for or a best fit for food truck operations.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WH