UPDATE companies SET description='The company designs and builds custom food trucks tailored to each cuisine, fabricating units that meet both road-legal and health-department standards. It also maintains a lineup of pre-built trucks for operators who want to launch quickly, and it provides consulting on business planning, cost management, and Washington Labor Industries compliance. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

Clients range from first-time entrepreneurs to established restaurants and catering companies adding a mobile unit. The firm cites restaurant and catering businesses as typical customers seeking to expand revenue through on-site catering and street vending.

Parisi frames the service as a guided tour that helps owners avoid the headaches he encountered, emphasizing that every truck is engineered around the specific menu and workflow rather than a one-size-fits-all template. The company also promotes a fast-tracked path to state legalization, positioning its compliance guidance as a way to prevent fines and delays.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom food truck design and fabrication", "Pre-built food truck sales", "Washington Labor Industries compliance consulting", "Food truck business plan consulting", "Menu-specific workflow engineering"], "industries": ["Food service", "Restaurant", "Catering", "Mobile food vending"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom food trucks built to match specific cuisine types", "Pre-built food trucks for quick start", "Washington Labor Industries compliance guidance", "Consulting from experienced food truck operators", "Fast-tracked state legalization"], "facts_used": ["Seattle, Washington headquarters -> db", "Owner Nick Parisi with 30+ years experience -> page ''/''", "Custom food truck design and build -> page ''/''", "Pre-built food trucks for sale -> page ''/''", "Washington LI compliance consulting -> page ''/''", "Business plan consulting -> page ''/''", "Serves restaurants and catering businesses -> page ''/''", "Fast-tracked state legalization -> page ''/services''", "Guided by food truck operators with experience -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "No two food trucks are identical, as we build to synchronize with the type and style of cuisine created.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-truck-northwest' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FoodPrep Solutions operates from its headquarters in Stamford, Connecticut. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in available materials.

The business provides an all-in-one service for food-service operations, combining weekly or biweekly knife sharpening and exchange with food equipment sales, maintenance, and merchandise. Its sharpening programs cover commercial knives, grinder knives, can openers, plates, bowl choppers, HCM and VCM blades, and slicer or food-processor blades. The company states it supplies 100 percent of the knives in its exchange program, eliminating customer purchases, and serves accounts ranging from independent groceries to national chains.

FoodPrep Solutions targets restaurants, delis, bakeries, supermarkets, food-processing plants, and food-service management companies. Its client examples include mom-and-pop groceries, nationwide chains, and top food-service management firms that rely on the firm for sharpening, equipment, maintenance, and merchandise.

