UPDATE companies SET description='Franklin Farms traces its roots to 1981, when it started on a mushroom farm in Franklin, Connecticut. The company is now headquartered in Boulder, Colorado. No founders are named in the source material, and ownership structure is not disclosed.

The company manufactures a wide range of plant-based proteins, including veggie burgers, breakfast items, veggie balls, seitan, tofu (organic super firm, organic, ready-bake kits), plant-powered meat, seasoned seitan, edamame, tempeh, fusion tofu, chickpea tofu and tempeh, and plant-based tuna. Production processes involve mixing, splicing, mingling, and dicing flavor-forward, high-quality plant proteins, with an explicit commitment to avoiding genetic engineering. Facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not published.

Its stated differentiation rests on non-GMO ingredient sourcing, flavor-forward formulations, and a product portfolio designed for both quick bites and sit-down dinners.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plant-based protein formulation", "Mixing and blending", "Seitan production", "Tofu manufacturing (organic and conventional)", "Tempeh fermentation", "Chickpea-based protein processing", "Plant-based meat analog extrusion/forming", "Product development and recipe innovation", "Non-GMO ingredient sourcing", "Flavor profiling and seasoning", "Ready-to-cook meal kit assembly"], "industries": ["Plant-based food manufacturing", "Vegetarian and vegan foods", "Retail food products", "Foodservice ingredients", "Natural and organic foods"], "materials": ["Organic soybeans", "Wheat gluten (seitan)", "Chickpeas", "Edamame", "Plant-based protein blends"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No genetic engineering in any product", "Flavor-forward, high-quality plant protein formulations", "Portfolio spans breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snack day parts", "\"Field to table\" sourcing narrative", "Focus on making plant-based cooking easy and delicious"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 on mushroom farm in Franklin, Connecticut -> /", "Headquarters Boulder, Colorado -> db", "Product list: veggie burgers, breakfast, veggie balls, seitan, tofu, tempeh, plant-based tuna, etc. -> /", "Processes: mixing, splicing, mingling, dicing, no genetic engineering -> /", "Differentiation: field to table, flavor-forward, health-conscious, non-GMO -> /", "Industries served: retail grocery, foodservice, plant-based foods -> /", "Materials inferred from product names: organic soybeans, wheat gluten, chickpeas, edamame -> /", "Capabilities derived from described processes and product range -> /", "Built_on differentiators from company statements -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Franklin Farms began in 1981 on a mushroom farm in Franklin, Connecticut. Since then, Franklin Farms has been bringing exciting yet good-for-you meatless meals from field to table.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='franklin-farms' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Franks Manufacturing operates from San Antonio, Texas, where the plant opened in 1980 as a family-owned venture producing Texas Best Lick Feeders for the agricultural liquid feed industry. The company remains family-owned and operated; ownership passed from father to son in November 2006, and James Franks serves as president.

The company specializes in heavy-gauge, high-volume thermoforming and vacuum forming of custom plastic products. Its capabilities include CNC routing on 3-axis machines handling sheets up to 60 by 120 inches, mold production, prototyping, and design services using MasterCAM and SolidWorks. Materials range from polyethylene and acrylics to non-ferrous metals such as aluminum, brass, and copper, as well as composites, foam, and wood-based boards. Franks describes itself as one of the largest custom vacuum formers in South Texas, serving both small and large volume orders.

Customers span agriculture, oil and gas, medical, grocery, construction, waste management, automotive, and government infrastructure. Concrete product lines include Protein Lick Feeders for agriculture, open-top containment tanks used in the Eagle Ford, Permian Basin, and Bakken shale fields, store bins for grocery retailers, and cough/sneeze shields for medical facilities. The client roster includes Fortune 500 companies.

Franks emphasizes a culture of teamwork, loyalty, respect, and integrity, aiming to deliver outstanding products with dedicated customer service. It holds SBA small business certification, veteran-owned status, and SCTRA, ESBE, SBE, and VBE certifications, and is a member of the San Antonio Manufacturers Association.', certifications=ARRAY['SBA Small Business','Veteran Owned','SCTRA certified (SCTRA # 2150611579)','Emerging Small Business Enterprise (ESBE)','Small Business Enterprise (SBE)','Veteran Business Enterprise (VBE)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Heavy-gauge thermoforming", "Vacuum forming", "CNC routing (3-axis, up to 60\" x 120\")", "Mold production", "Prototyping", "Design services (MasterCAM, SolidWorks)", "Acrylic fabrication", "CNC prototype molds", "Material selection (polyethylene, acrylics, non-ferrous metals, composites)", "Shipping and delivery (national and worldwide)"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Oil & Gas", "Medical", "Grocery", "Construction", "Waste Management", "Automotive", "Government Infrastructure", "Store Fixtures", "Ice and Beverage Products", "Packaging", "Secondary Containment", "Air Conditioning Parts"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Acrylics", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper", "Plastic", "Tooling foam", "Fiberglass", "Signboard", "Particleboard", "Oriented strand board", "Composites", "PVC", "Styrene", "ABS", "Non-abrasive materials"], "equipment": ["CNC routers (3-axis, up to 60\" x 120\", accommodates 5''x10'')", "MasterCAM software", "SolidWorks software"], "volume": "Small to large volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1980", "Veteran-owned and SBA small business certified", "Heavy-gauge, high-volume thermoforming specialist", "CNC routing up to 60\" x 120\" with MasterCAM/SolidWorks", "Nationwide and worldwide shipping"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 in San Antonio, Texas -> /about-us", "Family-owned, ownership passed father to son in 2006 -> /about-us", "James Franks president -> /about-us", "Specializes in heavy gauge high volume thermoforming -> /", "CNC routers 3-axis up to 60x120 inches -> /", "Materials: polyethylene, acrylics, aluminum, brass, copper, composites -> /", "Industries: agriculture, oil & gas, medical, grocery, construction, waste management, automobile, government infrastructure -> /", "Products: Protein Lick Feeders, Open Top Tanks, Store Bins, Cough/Sneeze Shields -> /", "Certifications: SBA Small Business, Veteran Owned, SCTRA, ESBE, SBE, VBE -> /about-us", "NAICS 326199, 326150 -> /about-us", "Member of San Antonio Manufacturers Association -> /about-us", "Shipping nationally and worldwide -> /", "Small and large volume market niche -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Franks Mfg. Co. specializes in heavy gauge, high volume thermoforming and custom plastic products.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='franks-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1998, Freedom Electronics operates from a 41,000-square-foot headquarters in Kennesaw, Georgia, with additional branches in Florida and Michigan. The company employs over 100 professionals, including engineers, certified technicians, and warehouse personnel, across its three locations.

The firm designs and manufactures engineered drop-in replacement parts for fuel dispensers and point-of-sale systems, including printers, displays, keyboards, and control boards. It also runs a remanufacturing program that applies advanced coatings and AI-enhanced inspection to extend component life, and manages a core-exchange system that credits customers for returned units.

Freedom Electronics serves distributors, technicians, and station owners in the retail petroleum industry. Its product line covers major dispenser brands such as Gilbarco, Wayne, VeriFone, Tokheim, Bennett, and Gasboy, providing both new aftermarket components and remanufactured assemblies.

The company emphasizes engineering innovations—advanced coatings, improved inspection technologies, and artificial intelligence integration—to produce more durable remanufactured parts that lower maintenance costs for retailers. A core-charge refund policy and dedicated technical support round out its service offering.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Remanufacturing of fuel dispenser components", "Engineered drop-in replacement part design", "Advanced coating application", "Automated inspection and testing", "Core exchange and refurbishment", "PCB/control board repair and replacement", "Printer replacement manufacturing", "Display replacement manufacturing", "Keyboard/keypad replacement manufacturing", "PPU display manufacturing", "Intercom and POS component supply", "Aftermarket parts distribution for major OEM brands"], "industries": ["Retail petroleum", "Fuel dispensing equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> /about", "Headquarters in Kennesaw, GA, 41,000 sq ft -> /about", "Branches in Florida and Michigan -> /about", "Over 100 employees -> /about", "Engineers and manufactures Freedom Engineered Products (drop-in replacements) -> /", "Remanufacturing with advanced coatings, improved inspection, AI integration -> /", "Core exchange program with credit -> /", "Serves distributors, technicians, station owners in retail petroleum industry -> /", "Carries major brands: Gilbarco, Wayne, VeriFone, Tokheim, Bennett, Gasboy -> /", "Product categories: printers, displays, keyboards, control boards, PPU displays, intercoms -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Freedom Engineered Products... best-in-class solutions for reduced inventory, higher quality, and profitability for distributors, technicians, and station owners in the retail petroleum industry.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count":