UPDATE companies SET description='Coextruded Plastic Technologies (CPT) Inc., operating as GO GREEN Food Packaging Solutions, was founded in 2001 in Janesville, Wisconsin. The company began with the founders'' entrepreneurial drive to develop green thermoforming capabilities for packaging.

The company manufactures thermoformed trays and lidding solutions for food and medical packaging. Its proprietary Go Green thermoforming technology reduces carbon footprint by up to 28% compared to conventional methods. Product lines include GO-POLYPRO™ polypropylene trays, GO-PAPER™ paper-based trays, GO-VSP™ vacuum skin packaging, and GO-OVERWRAP™ overwrap solutions, as well as pre-padded trays in various colors and compartment configurations. The company holds several patents for its tray designs, such as the Zazin tray with beveled sidewalls that save 40% in cube space.

GO GREEN serves the food packaging and medical packaging sectors. Its solutions address needs such as extended shelf life, modified atmosphere packaging (MAP), vacuum skin packaging (VSP), oven- and microwave-safe trays, and sustainability goals including recyclability and reduced carbon footprint.

The company was founded to pioneer environmentally responsible thermoforming. It differentiates itself with capabilities such as the only polypropylene tray that can be registered printed, a Flex Flange design compatible with conventional overwrap equipment, and a thermoforming process that cuts carbon emissions by up to 28%. The Zazin tray’s beveled sidewall design reduces shipping volume by 40%, offering supply chain savings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoforming", "Coextrusion", "Registered printing on polypropylene", "Flex Flange overwrap", "Vacuum skin packaging (VSP)", "Modified atmosphere packaging (MAP)", "Pre-padded tray production", "Compartment tray production", "Zazin tray design (beveled sidewall)", "Carbon footprint reduction thermoforming"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Medical packaging"], "materials": ["Polypropylene", "Paper", "Plastic films"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only polypropylene tray that can be registered printed", "Flex Flange overwrap compatible with conventional films and equipment", "Thermoforming technology reduces carbon footprint up to 28% versus conventional processes", "Zazin tray beveled sidewall design saves 40% cube space for freight and supply chain savings"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> /about", "Headquarters Janesville, Wisconsin -> db", "Manufactures thermoformed trays for food and medical packaging -> /about", "Proprietary Go Green thermoforming technology reduces carbon footprint up to 28% -> /about", "Product lines GO-POLYPRO, GO-PAPER, GO-VSP, GO-OVERWRAP -> /", "Pre-Padded Trays assortment -> /", "Unique capabilities: registered printing on PP, Flex Flange, Zazin Trays -> /about", "Industries: food packaging, medical packaging -> /about", "Focus on sustainability, EPR, MAP vs VSP, oven/microwave, fresh/frozen -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CPT\u2019s Go Green trays are used for a wide range of food and medical packaging applications.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='go-green-food-packaging-solutions-from-cpt-coextruded-plastic-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='GTX Manufacturing, LLC operates from Clay City, Kentucky, where it provides contract manufacturing services specializing in wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and electromechanical assemblies. The company describes itself as a full-service contract manufacturer with over 40 years of combined experience among its personnel.

The shop’s core capabilities include wire harness assembly (with harnesses exceeding 300 circuits), cable assembly, semi-automatic crimping, ultrasonic wire splicing (Sonobond), inkjet and hot-stamp wire marking (using a KIP 20 machine), connector overmolding and rubber injection molding for environmental protection, potting and encapsulating, J-STD-001 soldering, IPC-620A workmanship, 100% electrical testing on Cirris equipment, reverse engineering, and general box-build assembly. Prototyping and low-run production are offered alongside volume work.

GTX serves customers in automotive, heavy-equipment, trailer, and trucking markets, producing engine and chassis harnesses, trailer harnesses, dump-truck harnesses, and heavy-equipment harnesses. The company works with major connector brands such as Deutsch, Molex, Tyco, Yazaki, Sumitomo, and JST.

