UPDATE companies SET description='Grand Hawaii Electric LLC operates from Honolulu, Hawaii. Founder Johny Le, a licensed C‑13 electrical contractor, started the company after a decade crews on major O‘ahu projects — among them the Waikīkī International Market Place redevelopment, the Ae‘o and Whole Foods Ward high‑rise, the HART rail stations, and military work at Fort Shafter and the DISA Project. Le’s background includes a carpentry degree from Honolulu Community College (2008‑2010) and apprenticeship through IBEW 1186 and Associated Builders and Contractors.

The firm provides electrical repairs, troubleshooting, panel replacements, outlet and switch upgrades, LED lighting installations, EV charger installations, and general electrical contracting for residential and light‑commercial customers. It does not take on new‑construction work, focusing on service, maintenance, and retrofit projects across O‘ahu. Precision tools such as Leica Geosystem layout machines are used for complex installations.

The founder’s project history also references high‑rise residential towers (A‘ali‘i, Central Ala Moana, Sky Ala Moana), healthcare (Tripler Hospital), and transit (HART Rail), though current operations center on service calls and upgrades.

